<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Axiom Power Services is an engineering contractor based in Lagos, working on steam and gas turbines, industrial generating sets and the pumps, gearboxes, fans and compressors that sit in the same trains. Our engineers mobilise to plants in <a href="/turbine-services-lagos/">Lagos</a>, <a href="/turbine-services-port-harcourt/">Port Harcourt</a>, <a href="/turbine-services-warri/">Warri</a>, <a href="/turbine-services-abuja/">Abuja</a>, <a href="/turbine-services-kaduna/">Kaduna</a> and <a href="/turbine-services-kano/">Kano</a>. The work itself is the unglamorous end of power generation: outage execution, condition assessment, clearance restoration, alignment, balancing and recommissioning.</p><p>The plant we are usually called to has run well past its inspection window. History files are incomplete, clearance sheets from the last outage cannot be found, the vibration data stops at a monitor that was never trended, and the spares that were listed two outages ago were never ordered. That is the normal starting position in Nigerian industry, and a contractor who cannot work from it is of no use to a maintenance manager. So we begin by establishing what the machine is actually doing rather than what the manual says it should be doing.</p><p>Diagnosis comes before disassembly. Operating hours, trip and start counts, first stage and stage to stage pressures, heat rate drift, bearing metal temperatures, lube oil analysis and a borescope survey tell us whether the loss of output is deposits on the blading, solid particle erosion at the HP nozzles, moisture erosion in the last LP stages, worn gland and interstage seals, a condenser pulling air, or a fault that is not in the turbine at all. On generating sets the same discipline applies to load bank behaviour, exhaust temperature spread, blow by, coolant and oil condition, alternator insulation resistance and polarisation index. Naming the failure mode before opening the machine is what keeps an outage from becoming an open ended discovery exercise.</p><p>Quality control is written down or it did not happen. Work runs to agreed hold points, as found and as left clearances go on signed sheets, NDT results and balance data are recorded against the component they belong to, and vibration acceptance is judged against ISO 20816 and the OEM or API criteria for the machine rather than the feel of a bearing housing. Every job closes with a dossier that the next engineer can plan from: clearance records, alignment figures, inspection reports, spares consumed and a fresh baseline. If you want the condition of a unit established before you commit to any scope, start with a <a href="/power-plant-audit-nigeria/">power plant audit</a>, then request a technical proposal on info@axiompowerng.com or +234 803 000 0000.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">How We Work</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What You Can Expect</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Condition First, Scope Second</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">We do not price a scope from a machine description and a phone call. Operating hours, trip and start history, vibration trends, stage pressures, oil analysis and a borescope survey come first, and the scope of work is written against what that data shows. Where records are missing, a plant assessment establishes the baseline before anything is quoted.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">A Scope Priced Line by Line</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Each proposal carries a scope of work, a bill of quantities, an outage bar chart with float shown, a manpower schedule and a pre agreed rate for work found during disassembly. A procurement officer can compare it against a competing submission item by item instead of weighing two lump sums. When a wiped thrust pad or a cracked disc rim is found mid outage, it is priced against the agreed rate rather than stalling the job while commercial terms are reopened.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Acceptance Against Published Limits</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Clearances are restored to drawing, alignment is confirmed cold and verified hot with thermal growth allowances applied, and vibration is accepted against ISO 20816 and the OEM or API criteria applicable to the machine. As found and as left figures are recorded and signed at each hold point, including the ones that are within tolerance. Handover is a dossier of clearance sheets, NDT reports, balance data and a fresh vibration baseline, not a verbal sign off at the gate.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Lead Times Planned, Not Discovered</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Blading, diaphragms, bearing sets and rotor repairs are manufactured items with a production queue in front of them, and Form M, PAAR and port clearance sit on top of that. We split the work into confirmed, probable and contingency scope so long lead items are ordered against the first two categories months before the window opens. Consumables, gaskets, fasteners, seal strips and bearing spares are held at site before the crew mobilises so no day of downtime is spent waiting on a courier.</p>
      </div>
</div>
